TLDR: added actuator root url to security configuration to allow actuator endpoint discovery

Currently, when a project registers itself at a Spring Boot Admin (SBA from now) server for monitoring, SBA tries to find the exposed endpoints to monitor. As the endpoint is currently not accessible (due to security config) SBA falls back to a  [`ProbeEndpointsStrategy`](https://github.com/codecentric/spring-boot-admin/blob/master/spring-boot-admin-server/src/main/java/de/codecentric/boot/admin/server/config/AdminServerAutoConfiguration.java#L106).

This is less reliable and can result in, in cases where the backend service is rebooting, 200 OK responses for all endpoints resulting in non-exposed endpoints to be registered with SBA. As such, this PR adds configuration to expose the root actuator URL that provides a list of exposed endpoints, such as:

```
{
  "_links": {
    "self": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/management",
      "templated": false
    },
    "health-path": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/management/health/{*path}",
      "templated": true
    },
    "health": {
      "href": "http://localhost:8080/management/health",
      "templated": false
    },
    ....
```

This will fix SBA registering inaccessible endpoints resulting in UI errors.

